/code-review high — loop R1-late1, round 2 — range 26bfccee..020cf0f1 (branch 2026-10-08-execute-renders-served-at-a-url)

I found 9 issues in `26bfccee..020cf0f1`, with `docs/plans/` left out. These are unverified, as the recall-mode recipe says: nothing was run, and every finding comes from reading the code.

The three most important:
- **Case-insensitive file match (most severe):** on macOS, two names that differ only in case land on the same image file. The render copy compares file paths as exact strings, so it keeps the old entry. The server then shows the new image under the old state.
- **`?state=default`:** this URL used to 404 and now shows the default image as its own state. The mockup side doesn't do the same, so the frame and the other window come up empty, and comments split between `state: default` and `state: ""`.
- **No more pruning:** renders of screens that left the route map now stay on disk and in `renders.json` for good. If one of those codes later comes back at the same route, the server shows the old image again.

